@startuml uc-remove-member
!include _theme.iuml

state removeMember as "removeMember()" {

  state " " as NamingOnePerson
  state " " as Guarding
  state " " as Asking
  state " " as Removing

  [*] --> NamingOnePerson
  note on link
  <b>Operator</b> names one login to take out of the
  organisation
  end note

  NamingOnePerson --> Guarding
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> refuses two people whatever else is true
  • the only remaining owner, because an organisation
    with no owners cannot be administered by anybody
  • the account this run is authenticated as, because it
    could not put itself back
  Neither is an API error: GitHub performs both happily
  end note

  Guarding --> Asking
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> says which of the two states it found — an
  active membership, or an invitation never answered —
  and what will be lost
  end note

  Asking --> Removing
  note on link
  <b>Operator</b> confirms
  end note

  Removing --> [*]
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> removes them, and says that any membership
  held through an enterprise team is unaffected and has
  to be removed there
  end note
}

removeMember --> CONFIGURATION_RESOLVED
note on link
a guard exits 4 and nothing is attempted;
declining exits 1; somebody who is neither
a member nor invited is reported and exits 0
end note
@enduml
